WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:04.900
World Masterpiece Theater

00:07.800 --> 00:14.400
Homeless Child Remy

00:07.800 --> 00:14.400
"About Love"

00:15.260 --> 00:23.200
I continue wishing to see you

00:23.690 --> 00:28.360
Today we'll go on a journey

00:28.450 --> 00:32.310
That's as endless as the blue sky

00:32.820 --> 00:40.990
With joy, sorrow and hope come setbacks

00:41.360 --> 00:46.040
They repeat, they repeat

00:46.280 --> 00:50.870
What should I believe?

00:51.510 --> 00:59.880
You know nothing about love, however

01:00.320 --> 01:08.900
Someday you will feel warmth inside

01:09.730 --> 01:19.860
I dream of the day when you'll speak of love

01:20.860 --> 01:28.660
Tomorrow, our journey will begin

01:29.510 --> 01:35.000
Presented by:
Takara Fansubs & Migoto

01:35.040 --> 01:39.870
Episode 23:
Both of their Wishes

01:41.210 --> 01:45.810
After leaving Paris, we worked in a grape vineyard.

01:46.100 --> 01:48.380
We picked grapes for making wine.

01:53.130 --> 01:59.570
It was Mattia who rescued me from the mine when I got trapped.

02:02.260 --> 02:05.140
Mattia is always protecting me.

02:11.240 --> 02:12.160
Hey!

02:12.620 --> 02:13.700
Quit slacking off!

02:14.230 --> 02:15.790
Don't just stand here!

02:40.480 --> 02:42.600
All right. Let's take a break.

02:43.240 --> 02:45.540
Oh... I'm tired.

02:55.570 --> 02:57.610
Traveling performers!

02:58.010 --> 03:00.860
Come and watch our performance!
It'll be fun!

03:00.870 --> 03:02.340
We'll be waiting!

03:19.110 --> 03:20.240
Mattia!

03:20.660 --> 03:22.140
Huh?

03:25.460 --> 03:26.510
Let's go.

03:33.730 --> 03:36.180
This bread is really good.

03:55.400 --> 03:56.550
Mattia?

03:57.610 --> 04:00.340
What's wrong?
You haven't eaten your lunch.

04:00.880 --> 04:02.430
I don't want it.

04:02.500 --> 04:04.660
You've been acting a bit strange lately.

04:04.690 --> 04:07.630
No, I haven't.
- Did something happen?

04:10.010 --> 04:13.410
I want to be a violinist.

04:13.430 --> 04:14.230
Huh?

04:15.420 --> 04:18.530
My dad earned money playing his violin.

04:19.590 --> 04:24.030
So I grew up listening to my dad's violin.

04:24.890 --> 04:31.450
My dad told me I had talent and let me practice.

04:31.910 --> 04:37.040
I loved playing the violin with my dad.

04:37.510 --> 04:40.050
It was the best time ever.

04:46.570 --> 04:49.680
When my dad died, I couldn't play it anymore.

04:51.350 --> 04:56.240
I had to make a living, so I didn't even think about playing the violin

04:56.600 --> 05:01.120
while I was at the orphanage or with the circus or Gaspard.

05:05.130 --> 05:07.110
But...

05:07.560 --> 05:11.630
Since you gave me that violin, it's all I can think about.

05:12.170 --> 05:15.890
I love that violin. I want to practice more so I can play it better.

05:16.010 --> 05:18.770
I want to become a violinist like my dad.

05:19.300 --> 05:20.130
But...

05:20.550 --> 05:25.140
I can't do that if I keep staying at Gaspard's place. It's impossible.

05:30.410 --> 05:34.760
I heard that this lake makes people's wishes come true.

05:36.180 --> 05:40.930
A long time ago, the rivers and wells in this village had gone dry.

05:40.970 --> 05:43.230
The suffering people prayed for help,

05:43.690 --> 05:49.020
then an angel, Michael, came down from the sky and filled the lake with water.

05:49.510 --> 05:52.740
Since then, this lake has never gone dry.

05:53.420 --> 05:59.610
So they say if you pray at this lake, your wish will come true.

05:59.630 --> 06:02.750
It's just a myth, isn't it?
- Could be.

06:03.220 --> 06:11.250
But if it is true, then I wish for you to become a violinist.

06:16.840 --> 06:18.290
Remy...

06:24.280 --> 06:28.730
And I wish for you to find your real mother.

06:29.030 --> 06:30.240
My mother?

06:43.670 --> 06:45.670
This is Groussinou Avenue.

06:46.980 --> 06:49.680
Remy lives at Gaspard's house.

06:51.580 --> 06:53.730
Hey you!

06:54.420 --> 06:56.730
Go away!

06:57.720 --> 07:00.100
Remy lives in a place like this?

07:09.080 --> 07:11.810
Hello, is Mr. Gaspard here?

07:12.550 --> 07:16.160
<i>I'll finally get to see Remy.</i>
- Who is it?

07:20.990 --> 07:23.910
Hello.
- Who are you?

07:24.040 --> 07:26.320
I'm Blair, a lawyer.

07:26.350 --> 07:28.300
What's a lawyer doing here?

07:28.320 --> 07:30.930
We heard that a girl named Remy lives here.

07:31.430 --> 07:33.420
Who are you guys?

07:33.860 --> 07:36.430
I'm Mary, I work for the Milligan family.

07:37.750 --> 07:40.000
Say she's here, what do you want with her?

07:40.180 --> 07:43.020
She's here, isn't she?
And Mr. Vitalis too, right?

07:43.580 --> 07:45.270
Vitalis?

07:45.460 --> 07:47.020
No... He's dead.

07:48.760 --> 07:50.250
Oh no...

07:51.500 --> 07:53.280
Then what about Miss Remy?

07:54.590 --> 07:56.350
Miss Remy?

07:58.520 --> 08:00.640
Why don't you come in?

08:05.750 --> 08:09.380
That's why we're looking for Miss Remy.

08:09.730 --> 08:11.560
I understand your situation.

08:11.590 --> 08:13.800
But Remy is not here right now.

08:14.300 --> 08:16.810
Not here? Then where is she?

08:18.250 --> 08:20.810
She's gone to the countryside for her performance business.

08:23.270 --> 08:25.810
Could you tell me where?

08:26.350 --> 08:32.530
Huh, I don't know if I can contact her or not since they'll be moving around a lot.

08:32.970 --> 08:34.820
We really need to see Remy.

08:36.500 --> 08:38.610
All right, I'll take care of it.

08:38.620 --> 08:41.250
But it will take some time.

08:44.140 --> 08:45.220
Thank you.

08:45.250 --> 08:47.860
Please let us know if you receive any information.

08:56.710 --> 08:59.120
Remy is a rich girl?

08:59.190 --> 09:01.940
On top of that she's a daughter of the British Milligan family.

09:05.160 --> 09:08.570
It seems like luck has come my way.

09:08.740 --> 09:11.600
If I handle things carefully, I could get some good money.

09:12.340 --> 09:15.370
Do you think that man will find Remy?

09:15.630 --> 09:18.030
Right now, Gaspard's the only one we can rely on.

09:18.060 --> 09:20.450
We just have to wait.
- Yes.

09:59.230 --> 10:01.320
You're very talented.

10:01.350 --> 10:03.780
Where did you learn the violin?

10:05.900 --> 10:09.670
You...
-Mattia wasn't taught the violin.

10:10.050 --> 10:11.920
But he's very good at it.

10:12.230 --> 10:15.610
Oh... Do you guys live in the village?

10:15.630 --> 10:16.580
No.

10:16.690 --> 10:20.340
I'm...
- Remy, it's time to go back to the vineyard.

10:20.660 --> 10:21.600
Wait!

10:23.800 --> 10:25.090
Bye!

10:44.250 --> 10:46.760
Don't splash me, Remy!

10:46.780 --> 10:48.750
You're splashing, Lise!

10:49.050 --> 10:51.250
You're excited, aren't you?

10:51.750 --> 10:53.570
So are you, Marie!

10:54.770 --> 10:57.120
Mr. Remon, who are those kids?

10:59.240 --> 11:03.040
Oh... They're here from Paris to work.

11:03.070 --> 11:06.010
I hire them every year from Gaspard.

11:06.050 --> 11:10.210
Gaspard takes in homeless children and finds them work.

11:10.360 --> 11:12.530
Homeless children?

11:20.020 --> 11:21.200
That boy...

11:32.940 --> 11:34.540
Big brother Mattia!

11:41.550 --> 11:44.510
Hey, hey! Quit slacking off! Get to work! To work!

11:44.540 --> 11:45.270
Yes, ma'am.

11:45.990 --> 11:46.910
You!

11:48.990 --> 11:51.440
My name's Alberto.

11:51.480 --> 11:54.380
I teach violin at a school in Paris.

11:55.430 --> 11:57.570
You like the violin, don't you?

11:59.460 --> 12:03.000
Would you like to play this song?

12:04.010 --> 12:05.890
Here, take a look.

12:11.200 --> 12:15.040
This is a song that the great composer Mozart wrote.

12:18.840 --> 12:21.080
Don't tell me, you can't read sheet music?

12:24.210 --> 12:28.100
Oh, I see.
You memorize the song by ear.

12:28.680 --> 12:33.300
If you do that, then you won't be able to play songs you've never heard before.

12:34.760 --> 12:39.440
There's many songs in the world you've never heard.

12:40.510 --> 12:44.450
Once you're able to read sheet music, then you can play any song.

12:44.480 --> 12:45.330
Even this one.

12:48.040 --> 12:50.320
I could teach you how to read sheet music.

12:51.270 --> 12:53.360
I...
- Hey, Mattia!

12:53.380 --> 12:54.840
Mattia, where are you?

12:55.650 --> 12:56.840
I should go.

13:09.940 --> 13:12.340
Big brother Mattia's late.

13:12.370 --> 13:15.780
He is.
- Big brother Mattia seems strange lately.

13:16.500 --> 13:19.430
He always looks angry and deep in thought.

13:19.490 --> 13:23.840
He used to play with us a lot more.
- Yeah...

13:29.400 --> 13:33.290
<i>Once you're able to read sheet music, then you can play any song.</i>

14:40.820 --> 14:43.450
It's wonderful. Just wonderful.

14:44.560 --> 14:45.820
Yeah.

14:51.290 --> 14:55.650
If you practice more, you'll be able to play just like him.

14:55.830 --> 15:00.180
He's a real musician. I'll never be like him no matter what I do.

15:00.680 --> 15:02.830
Don't give up!

15:04.860 --> 15:05.500
Oh...

15:08.250 --> 15:09.560
Wait!

15:11.000 --> 15:12.340
I'd like to talk to you.

15:14.330 --> 15:17.600
Remy, go back.
- But...

15:18.710 --> 15:19.730
Go, please.

15:21.550 --> 15:22.550
Okay...

15:33.780 --> 15:36.080
Don't you want to come with me?

15:36.630 --> 15:37.160
Huh?

15:37.680 --> 15:39.520
You have talent.

15:39.760 --> 15:43.520
It'd be a waste to hide it.

15:43.540 --> 15:45.690
It's not impossible to become a world famous violinist,

15:45.710 --> 15:48.820
if you study music from the basics.

15:50.640 --> 15:52.890
I'm leaving here tomorrow.

15:52.930 --> 15:57.900
If you want to come with me, I'll happily teach you everything I know.

16:10.470 --> 16:12.870
<i>I could study music.</i>

16:12.890 --> 16:17.570
<i>If I go with him, I'll be able to play the violin whenever I want.</i>

16:31.190 --> 16:34.050
I wonder what he wants to talk to Mattia about?

16:34.630 --> 16:35.870
I don't know.

16:36.090 --> 16:38.560
But it seemed like something important.

16:40.420 --> 16:45.490
I'm worried. I feel like big brother Mattia won't come back anymore.

16:45.490 --> 16:49.070
Huh?
- Big brother Mattia seems strange lately.

16:49.550 --> 16:53.190
Silly... Where would Mattia go?

16:53.210 --> 16:56.080
Right, Remy?
- Hmmm...

17:00.550 --> 17:05.170
No way! Mattia's not someone who'd abandon us.

17:05.300 --> 17:08.210
He wouldn't do that.
- I wouldn't mind.

17:08.520 --> 17:09.220
Huh?

17:09.700 --> 17:12.800
I don't mind. I don't mind if Mattia doesn't mind.

17:15.910 --> 17:17.110
No!

17:17.130 --> 17:21.020
I don't want him to go! I don't!
- I don't either.

17:21.040 --> 17:24.000
Me either.
- Me either.

17:24.030 --> 17:25.230
I don't either!

17:25.520 --> 17:26.700
Me either!

17:28.540 --> 17:31.780
What? You guys still up?

17:33.360 --> 17:35.420
Big brother Mattia!

17:36.740 --> 17:40.330
Big brother Mattia! We'll be together forever, right?

17:40.370 --> 17:42.160
We'll all be together forever, right?

18:04.830 --> 18:07.250
Mattia, come with me.

18:08.180 --> 18:11.650
I'll teach you everything I know.

18:12.000 --> 18:16.160
I'll go. I'll go with you!
I want to learn the violin!

18:16.820 --> 18:20.440
I love the violin! I want to practice more and get better at it!

18:20.480 --> 18:22.990
I want to become a violinist like my dad!

18:25.440 --> 18:26.030
Huh?

18:32.810 --> 18:34.260
My name's Remy.

18:36.450 --> 18:38.430
Don't do things you know are wrong, Mattia!

18:38.870 --> 18:40.690
I'm not doing them because I want to!

18:40.720 --> 18:43.620
I can't survive without doing them!

18:44.260 --> 18:45.480
Mattia...

18:45.590 --> 18:47.440
I...

18:48.310 --> 18:50.820
Remy! Remy!

18:51.300 --> 18:53.310
Wait, Remy!

18:53.940 --> 18:56.690
Don't go, Remy!

19:03.540 --> 19:04.790
Mattia...

19:06.480 --> 19:07.790
Were you having a bad dream?

19:11.000 --> 19:12.060
Remy!

19:42.840 --> 19:44.660
<i>Big brother Mattia!</i>

19:45.150 --> 19:48.150
<i>Mattia's not someone who'd abandon us.</i>

20:10.290 --> 20:13.070
Are you sure that's your decision?

20:13.230 --> 20:14.690
Did you think it over well?

20:16.350 --> 20:19.700
I can't go without Remy or my friends. They're all my friends.

20:20.100 --> 20:22.670
Yes, friends are important.

20:23.040 --> 20:26.230
But this will affect your entire future.

20:26.260 --> 20:27.760
I've already made up my mind.

20:29.320 --> 20:30.380
Mattia!

20:31.860 --> 20:34.720
I teach at the Couteau music academy in Paris.

20:35.300 --> 20:38.290
If you change your mind, come and see me anytime.

20:52.890 --> 20:56.210
Let us stay together forever.

20:57.860 --> 21:00.440
I want to be with Remy.

21:01.080 --> 21:02.160
Huh...

21:09.200 --> 21:11.080
We'll be together forever.

21:11.690 --> 21:13.590
We'll never be apart.

21:15.610 --> 21:16.580
We'll never be apart.

21:18.130 --> 21:18.850
Remy...

21:27.240 --> 21:31.780
<i>Madam, I finally got some information about your daughter, Remy.</i>

21:31.990 --> 21:35.650
<i>Your daughter is living at Gaspard's house.</i>

21:36.100 --> 21:39.650
<i>I'll find her soon and bring her back to you. So please wait.</i>

21:43.420 --> 21:47.700
I wonder if that guy will really find Remy.

21:47.860 --> 21:49.410
Can we really trust him?

21:55.430 --> 22:04.620
Surely, not everyone can be so strong

22:05.260 --> 22:16.220
The blue sky lifts all of the world's tears...

22:16.680 --> 22:26.360
Tomorrow's courage comes

22:26.590 --> 22:36.250
From the future that gives us our fate

22:36.420 --> 22:45.260
Try to seek for them more

22:46.110 --> 22:49.840
Give your heart to

22:49.960 --> 23:03.490
That person who is also seeking you

23:18.560 --> 23:20.370
Why are you looking for Remy?

23:20.580 --> 23:24.720
Because Remy is a daughter of the Milligan family.

23:24.910 --> 23:26.170
Come here, Remy!

23:27.420 --> 23:29.670
Remy! Remy!

23:29.900 --> 23:32.470
Mattia! Mattia!

23:32.490 --> 23:36.430
<i>Love Torn Apart</i>

23:32.490 --> 23:36.430
Next time:
